# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've now discussed three different ways to represent channels in mathematical terms, namely Stinespring representations, Kraus representations, and Choi representations.\n"
"We also have the definition of a channel, which states that a channel is a linear mapping that always transforms density matrices into density matrices, even when the channel is applied to just part of a compound system.\n"
"The remainder of the lesson is devoted to a mathematical proof that the three representations are equivalent and precisely capture the definition.\n"
msgstr ""
"ناقشنا حتى الآن ثلاث طرق مختلفة لتمثيل القنوات رياضياً، وهي تمثيلات ستينسبرينغ، وتمثيلات كراوس، وتمثيلات تشوي.\n"
"كما لدينا تعريف القناة، الذي يشترط أن تكون القناة تحويلاً خطياً يحوّل دائماً مصفوفات الكثافة إلى مصفوفات كثافة، حتى حين تُطبَّق القناة على جزء فقط من نظام مركّب.\n"
"الجزء المتبقي من الدرس مكرّس لإثبات رياضي بأن التمثيلات الثلاثة متكافئة وتُعبّر بدقة عن التعريف.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview of the proof {#overview-of-the-proof}"
msgstr "نظرة عامة على البرهان {#overview-of-the-proof}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our goal is to establish the equivalence of a collection of four statements, and we'll begin by writing them down precisely.\n"
"All four statements follow the same conventions that have been used throughout the lesson, namely that $\\Phi$ is a linear mapping from square matrices to square matrices, the rows and columns of the input matrices have been placed in correspondence with the classical states of a system $\\mathsf{X}$ (the input system), and the rows and columns of the output matrices have been placed in correspondence with the classical states of a system $\\mathsf{Y}$ (the output system).\n"
msgstr ""
"هدفنا هو إثبات تكافؤ مجموعة من أربع عبارات، وسنبدأ بصياغتها بدقة.\n"
"تتبع العبارات الأربع الاصطلاحات المستخدمة طوال الدرس، وهي أن $\\Phi$ تحويل خطي من المصفوفات المربعة إلى المصفوفات المربعة، وأن صفوف وأعمدة مصفوفات المدخلات وُضعت بالتوافق مع الحالات الكلاسيكية لنظام $\\mathsf{X}$ (نظام المدخلات)، وأن صفوف وأعمدة مصفوفات المخرجات وُضعت بالتوافق مع الحالات الكلاسيكية لنظام $\\mathsf{Y}$ (نظام المخرجات).\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\Phi$ is a channel from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}$. That is, $\\Phi$ always transforms density matrices to density matrices, even when it acts on one part of a larger compound system.\n"
msgstr "$\\Phi$ قناة من $\\mathsf{X}$ إلى $\\mathsf{Y}$. أي أن $\\Phi$ تحوّل دائماً مصفوفات الكثافة إلى مصفوفات كثافة، حتى حين تعمل على جزء من نظام مركّب أكبر.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Choi matrix $J(\\Phi)$ is positive semidefinite and satisfies the condition $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"
msgstr "مصفوفة تشوي $J(\\Phi)$ شبه محددة موجبة وتحقق الشرط $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is a Kraus representation for $\\Phi$. That is, there exist matrices $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ for which the equation $\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}$ is true for every input $\\rho$, and that satisfy the condition $\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"
msgstr "يوجد تمثيل كراوس لـ$\\Phi$. أي توجد مصفوفات $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ تحقق المعادلة $\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}$ لكل مدخل $\\rho$، وتحقق الشرط $\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is a Stinespring representation for $\\Phi$. That is, there exist systems $\\mathsf{W}$ and $\\mathsf{G}$ for which the pairs $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ and $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$ have the same number of classical states, along with a unitary matrix $U$ representing a unitary operation from $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ to $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$, such that $\\Phi(\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}}\\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho) U^{\\dagger} \\bigr)$.\n"
msgstr "يوجد تمثيل ستينسبرينغ لـ$\\Phi$. أي توجد أنظمة $\\mathsf{W}$ و$\\mathsf{G}$ تتساوى فيهما الزوجان $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ و$(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$ في عدد الحالات الكلاسيكية، إلى جانب مصفوفة أحادية $U$ تمثّل عملية أحادية من $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ إلى $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$، بحيث $\\Phi(\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}}\\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho) U^{\\dagger} \\bigr)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The way the proof works is that a cycle of implications is proved:\n"
"the first statement in our list implies the second, the second implies the third, the third implies the fourth, and the fourth statement implies the first.\n"
"This establishes that all four statements are equivalent — which is to say that they're either all true or all false for a given choice of $\\Phi$ — because the implications can be followed transitively from any one statement to any other.\n"
msgstr ""
"تعتمد طريقة البرهان على إثبات دورة من الاستلزامات:\n"
"العبارة الأولى في قائمتنا تستلزم الثانية، والثانية تستلزم الثالثة، والثالثة تستلزم الرابعة، والرابعة تستلزم الأولى.\n"
"هذا يثبت أن العبارات الأربع متكافئة — أي أنها إما كلها صحيحة أو كلها خاطئة لأي اختيار معين لـ$\\Phi$ — لأن الاستلزامات يمكن اتباعها بشكل تعدّي من أي عبارة إلى أي عبارة أخرى.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is a common strategy when proving that a collection of statements are equivalent, and a useful trick to use in such a context is to set up the implications in a way that makes them as easy to prove as possible.\n"
"That is the case here — and in fact we've already encountered two of the four implications.\n"
msgstr ""
"هذه استراتيجية شائعة عند إثبات تكافؤ مجموعة من العبارات، وحيلة مفيدة في هذا السياق هي ترتيب الاستلزامات بطريقة تجعلها أسهل ما يمكن في الإثبات.\n"
"وهذا ما تم هنا بالفعل — وفي الواقع لقد صادفنا اثنين من الاستلزامات الأربعة سابقاً.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Channels to Choi matrices {#channels-to-choi-matrices}"
msgstr "من القنوات إلى مصفوفات تشوي {#channels-to-choi-matrices}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Referring to the statements listed above by their numbers, the first implication to be proved is 1 $\\Rightarrow$ 2.\n"
"This implication was already discussed in the context of the Choi state of a channel.\n"
"Here we'll summarize the mathematical details.\n"
msgstr ""
"بالإشارة إلى العبارات المذكورة أعلاه بأرقامها، الاستلزام الأول المراد إثباته هو 1 $\\Rightarrow$ 2.\n"
"ناقشنا هذا الاستلزام في سياق حالة تشوي للقناة.\n"
"سنلخص هنا التفاصيل الرياضية.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assume that the classical state set of the input system $\\mathsf{X}$ is $\\Sigma$ and let $n = \\vert\\Sigma\\vert$.\n"
"Consider the situation in which $\\Phi$ is applied to the second of two copies of $\\mathsf{X}$ together in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"افترض أن مجموعة الحالات الكلاسيكية لنظام المدخلات $\\mathsf{X}$ هي $\\Sigma$ وليكن $n = \\vert\\Sigma\\vert$.\n"
"خذ الوضع الذي تُطبَّق فيه $\\Phi$ على نسخة ثانية من نسختين من $\\mathsf{X}$ معاً في الحالة\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}} \\sum_{a \\in \\Sigma} \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}} \\sum_{a \\in \\Sigma} \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which, as a density matrix, is given by\n"
msgstr "والتي تُعطى كمصفوفة كثافة بالصيغة\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{a,b \\in \\Sigma}\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{a,b \\in \\Sigma}\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result can be written as\n"
msgstr "يمكن كتابة النتيجة على النحو التالي\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(\\operatorname{Id}\\otimes \\,\\Phi) \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\Phi\\bigl(\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{J(\\Phi)}{n},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(\\operatorname{Id}\\otimes \\,\\Phi) \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\Phi\\bigl(\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{J(\\Phi)}{n},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and by the assumption that $\\Phi$ is a channel this must be a density matrix.\n"
"Like all density matrices it must be positive semidefinite, and multiplying a positive semidefinite matrix by a positive real number yields another positive semidefinite matrix, and therefore $J(\\Phi) \\geq 0$.\n"
msgstr ""
"وبافتراض أن $\\Phi$ قناة، يجب أن يكون هذا مصفوفة كثافة.\n"
"كأي مصفوفة كثافة، يجب أن تكون شبه محددة موجبة، وضرب مصفوفة شبه محددة موجبة في عدد حقيقي موجب يعطي مصفوفة شبه محددة موجبة أخرى، لذا $J(\\Phi) \\geq 0$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Moreover, under the assumption that $\\Phi$ is a channel, it must preserve trace, and therefore\n"
msgstr "علاوة على ذلك، بافتراض أن $\\Phi$ قناة، يجب أن تحفظ الأثر، وبالتالي\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi))\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\Phi( \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert)\\bigr) \\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi))\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\Phi( \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert)\\bigr) \\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choi to Kraus representations {#choi-to-kraus-representations}"
msgstr "من تمثيلات تشوي إلى تمثيلات كراوس {#choi-to-kraus-representations}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second implication, again referring to the statements in our list by their numbers, is 2 $\\Rightarrow$ 3.\n"
"To be clear, we're ignoring the other statements — and in particular we cannot make the assumption that $\\Phi$ is a channel.\n"
"All we have to work with is that $\\Phi$ is a linear mapping whose Choi representation satisfies $J(\\Phi) \\geq 0$ and\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"الاستلزام الثاني، مع الإشارة مجدداً إلى العبارات في قائمتنا بأرقامها، هو 2 $\\Rightarrow$ 3.\n"
"للتوضيح، نحن نتجاهل العبارات الأخرى — ولا يمكننا بالتحديد افتراض أن $\\Phi$ قناة.\n"
"كل ما يمكننا الاستناد إليه هو أن $\\Phi$ تحويل خطي يحقق تمثيله بمصفوفة تشوي $J(\\Phi) \\geq 0$ والشرط $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This, however, is all we need to conclude that $\\Phi$ has a Kraus representation\n"
msgstr "هذا وحده كافٍ للاستنتاج بأن $\\Phi$ لها تمثيل كراوس\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for which the condition\n"
msgstr "يحقق الشرط\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "is satisfied.\n"
msgstr "نبدأ بالافتراض البالغ الأهمية بأن $J(\\Phi)$ شبه محددة موجبة، مما يعني إمكانية التعبير عنها على الشكل\n"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We begin with the critically important assumption that $J(\\Phi)$ is positive semidefinite, which means that it is possible to express it in the form\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "for some way of choosing the vectors $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle.$\n"
#| "In general there will be multiple ways to do this — and in fact this directly mirrors the freedom one has in choosing a Kraus representation for $\\Phi.$\n"
msgid ""
"for some way of choosing the vectors $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$.\n"
"In general there will be multiple ways to do this — and in fact this directly mirrors the freedom one has in choosing a Kraus representation for $\\Phi$.\n"
msgstr "إحدى طرق الحصول على مثل هذا التعبير هي استخدام مبرهنة الطيف أولاً للكتابة\n"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One way to obtain such an expression is to first use the spectral theorem to write\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\lambda_k \\vert \\gamma_k \\rangle \\langle \\gamma_k \\vert,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\lambda_k \\vert \\gamma_k \\rangle \\langle \\gamma_k \\vert,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "in which $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{N-1}$ are the eigenvalues of $J(\\Phi)$ (which are necessarily nonnegative real numbers because $J(\\Phi)$ is positive semidefinite) and $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\gamma_{N-1}\\rangle$ are unit eigenvectors corresponding to the eigenvalues $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{N-1}.$\n"
msgid "in which $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{N-1}$ are the eigenvalues of $J(\\Phi)$ (which are necessarily nonnegative real numbers because $J(\\Phi)$ is positive semidefinite) and $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\gamma_{N-1}\\rangle$ are unit eigenvectors corresponding to the eigenvalues $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{N-1}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"لاحظ أنه رغم عدم وجود حرية في اختيار القيم الذاتية (باستثناء ترتيبها)، هناك حرية في اختيار المتجهات الذاتية، لا سيما حين تكون هناك قيم ذاتية ذات تعدّدية أكبر من واحد (قيم ذاتية مكرّرة).\n"
"لذا، هذا ليس تعبيراً فريداً لـ$J(\\Phi)$ — نحن نفترض فقط وجود مثل هذا التعبير.\n"
"بصرف النظر عن ذلك، بما أن القيم الذاتية أعداد حقيقية غير سالبة، فإن لها جذوراً تربيعية غير سالبة، وبالتالي يمكننا اختيار\n"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that, while there's no freedom in choosing the eigenvalues (except for how they're ordered), there is freedom in the choice of the eigenvectors, particularly when there are eigenvalues with multiplicity larger than one.\n"
"So, this is not a unique expression of $J(\\Phi)$ — we're just assuming we have one such expression.\n"
"Regardless, because the eigenvalues are nonnegative real numbers, they have nonnegative square roots, and so we can select\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\lambda_k} \\vert \\gamma_k\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\lambda_k} \\vert \\gamma_k\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "for each $k = 0,\\ldots,N-1$ to obtain an expression of the form $(1).$\n"
msgid "for each $k = 0,\\ldots,N-1$ to obtain an expression of the form $(1)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"ليس ضرورياً أن يأتي التعبير $(1)$ من تحليل طيفي بهذه الطريقة، وبالتحديد لا يلزم أن تكون المتجهات $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ متعامدة بشكل عام.\n"
"والجدير بالملاحظة أنه يمكننا اختيار هذه المتجهات لتكون متعامدة إذا أردنا — وعلاوة على ذلك لا نحتاج أبداً أن يكون $N$ أكبر من $nm$\n"
"(مع التذكير بأن $n$ و$m$ يشيران إلى أعداد الحالات الكلاسيكية لـ$\\mathsf{X}$ و$\\mathsf{Y}$ على التوالي).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "It is, however, not essential that the expression $(1)$ comes from a spectral decomposition in this way, and in particular the vectors $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ need not be orthogonal in general.\n"
#| "It is noteworthy, though, that we can choose these vectors to be orthogonal if we wish — and moreover we never need $N$ to be larger than $nm$\n"
#| "(recalling that $n$ and $m$ denote the numbers of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y},$ respectively).\n"
msgid ""
"It is, however, not essential that the expression $(1)$ comes from a spectral decomposition in this way, and in particular the vectors $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ need not be orthogonal in general.\n"
"It is noteworthy, though, that we can choose these vectors to be orthogonal if we wish — and moreover we never need $N$ to be larger than $nm$\n"
"(recalling that $n$ and $m$ denote the numbers of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$, respectively).\n"
msgstr "بعد ذلك، يمكن تحليل كل من المتجهات $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ على النحو التالي\n"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, each of the vectors $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ can be further decomposed as\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where the vectors $\\{ \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle \\}$ have entries corresponding to the classical states of $\\mathsf{Y}$ and can be explicitly determined by the equation\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle = \\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}\\bigr) \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle = \\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}\\bigr) \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "for each $a\\in\\Sigma$ and $k=0,\\ldots,N-1.$\n"
#| "Although $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ are not necessarily unit vectors, this is the same process we would use to analyze what would happen if a standard basis measurement was performed on the system $\\mathsf{X}$ given a quantum state vector of the pair $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"
msgid ""
"for each $a\\in\\Sigma$ and $k=0,\\ldots,N-1$.\n"
"Although $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ are not necessarily unit vectors, this is the same process we would use to analyze what would happen if a standard basis measurement was performed on the system $\\mathsf{X}$ given a quantum state vector of the pair $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"
msgstr ""
"ونصل الآن إلى الحيلة التي تجعل هذا الجزء من البرهان ينجح.\n"
"نُعرّف مصفوفات كراوس $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ وفق المعادلة التالية.\n"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"And now we come to the trick that makes this part of the proof work.\n"
"We define our Kraus matrices $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ according to the following equation.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"A_k = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"A_k = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can think about this formula purely symbolically: $\\vert a\\rangle$ effectively gets flipped around to form $\\langle a\\vert$ and moved to right-hand side, forming a matrix.\n"
"For the purposes of verifying the proof, the formula is all we need.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "There is, however, a simple and intuitive relationship between the vector $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle$ and the matrix $A_k,$ which is that by *vectorizing* $A_k$ we get $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle.$\n"
#| "What it means to vectorize $A_k$ is that we stack the columns on top of one another (with the leftmost column on top proceeding to the rightmost on the bottom), in order to form a vector.\n"
#| "For instance, if $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are both qubits, and for some choice of $k$ we have\n"
msgid ""
"There is, however, a simple and intuitive relationship between the vector $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle$ and the matrix $A_k$, which is that by *vectorizing* $A_k$ we get $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle$.\n"
"What it means to vectorize $A_k$ is that we stack the columns on top of one another (with the leftmost column on top proceeding to the rightmost on the bottom), in order to form a vector.\n"
"For instance, if $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are both qubits, and for some choice of $k$ we have\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle & = \\alpha_{00} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{11} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle & = \\alpha_{00} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{11} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle & = \\alpha_{00} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{11} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
